# AWS CloudFormation – Lambda Function Deployment

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the deployment of an AWS Lambda function using an AWS CloudFormation template. The infrastructure was provisioned in the `us-east-1` region for the Nautilus DevOps team.

CloudFormation was used to create and configure the Lambda function and its IAM execution role.

## Project Objectives

- Create a CloudFormation template named `xfusion-lambda.yml`.
- Deploy a stack named `xfusion-lambda-app`.
- Create an AWS Lambda function named `xfusion-lambda`.
- Configure Python as the Lambda runtime.
- Set memory allocation to 128 MB.
- Configure the execution timeout to 10 seconds.
- Create and attach an IAM role named `lambda_execution_role`.
- Return HTTP status code 200 and the required response message.

